  "worked_solution": "Since the graph of $f(x)$ passes through $(3,-1)$, we have that $f(3)=-1.$ Therefore, the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $a=3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{\u2032}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(3)+{f}^{\u2032}(3)(x-3) \\\\  & =-1+2(x-3) \\\\  & =-1+2x-6 \\\\  & =2x-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
